WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.230
With the amount of research that must be done
within the SCP Foundation, including tests

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.740
on all the various anomalies currently in
containment, it is only natural for Foundation

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.349
staff to include some of the greatest scientific
minds in the multiverse.

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:19.470
Minds such as Dr. Jack Bright, who began his
career as human with only two outstanding

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:23.670
qualities: his keen intellect and his absurdly
poor luck.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:28.050
The latter of which eventually resulted in
his temporary demise and resurrection into

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:32.350
the technically disembodied consciousness
we know and love today.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:37.810
Though having his great mind transferred into
the anomalous medallion SCP-963 has only made

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:43.610
him more eccentric with time, Dr. Bright might
be the poster child for the ideal foundation

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.970
researcher: an out of the box thinker with
a flexible relationship to his own mortality

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.450
and morality.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:53.720
Of course, Bright isn’t the only man of
science out there who could be classified

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.360
as an anomaly.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.230
As a matter of fact, one particular man on
the Foundation’s radar could easily claim

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:05.400
such a status and then go beyond it with his
nasty habit of bragging about his accomplishments.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:11.450
That man is the self-proclaimed smartest being
in the universe: Rick Sanchez.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:15.390
Seemingly the unemployed live-in grandfather
of the middle-class Smith family, Rick spends

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:20.320
his spare time traveling freely between outer
space and different dimensions, assisted by

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:26.190
his signature portal gun and a metric buttload
of other gadgets of Sanchez’s own design.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:31.080
Rick Sanchez has been sought after by the
research team of SCP Foundation on three occasions

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.080
before.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.200
Once, when the elderly scientist was scouted
for a job interview which he famously didn’t

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.410
take seriously.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.440
According to one of the researchers present,
Sanchez would repeatedly belch in the middle

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.960
of his sentences and over the course of the
interview made several references to a supposed

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.590
“Cabin In The Woods.”

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:51.590
When asked to elaborate what he meant by those
remarks, Sanchez did not.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:57.240
This insubordination - combined with his gas
and bad attitude - ultimately cost him the

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.240
job.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.690
Several months later, the SCP Foundation would
discover that during the time that Sanchez

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:06.009
had been present for his interview, which
had taken place within Biological Containment

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:13.639
Site-103, the foul-tempered inventor had smuggled
several instances of SCP-2941 out of the facility

00:02:13.639 --> 00:02:18.099
in what Sanchez himself would later describe
as “one of those bags of holding, you know,

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:19.819
from dungeons and dragons.”

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:24.860
As those familiar with the Foundation’s
records would know, instances of SCP-2941

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:29.419
can be extremely dangerous outside of containment
due to the anomalous produce’s potential

00:02:29.419 --> 00:02:32.680
for explosive growth in conditions of increased
morale.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.819
It was a stroke of good fortune that when
Mobile Task Force Theta 4 A.K.A.

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:41.650
The Gardeners finally caught up with Sanchez
at his earthly home that all instances of

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:47.059
SCP-2941 were recorded as having lower morale
levels than had ever been recorded.

00:02:47.059 --> 00:02:51.349
According to Sanchez, he had injected the
instances with a specialized serum capable

00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:55.790
of inducing a state of permanent depression
in anything with a conscious mind.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:58.650
To quote Sanchez, “I fixed your dumb fruit
problem.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.650
You’re welcome.”

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:04.129
While both of the previous occasions were
mostly unpleasant for any SCP Foundation staff

00:03:04.129 --> 00:03:08.129
involved and better left forgotten, it was
the third encounter with Rick Sanchez where

00:03:08.129 --> 00:03:13.159
the man went from a minor annoyance to a being
capable of threatening the Foundation’s

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.260
very existence.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:19.680
It all started, as is often enough the case
when misfortune arises, when Dr. Bright got

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.980
one of his infamous out-of-the-box ideas.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:27.989
The immortal researcher was reviewing the
data from the SCP-2941 case, and realized

00:03:27.989 --> 00:03:32.949
that it might be possible for the Foundation
to use Sanchez to neutralize other – more

00:03:32.949 --> 00:03:35.309
overtly hostile – anomalies.

00:03:35.309 --> 00:03:39.129
Specifically, SCP-682 - the hard to destroy
reptile.

00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:44.519
While everything that the Foundation had previously
thrown at SCP-682 had done little more than

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:49.459
increase its aggression, Dr. Bright imagined
that a man as unpredictable as Rick Sanchez

00:03:49.459 --> 00:03:53.979
might have an invention that could at least
weaken the reptile or otherwise reduce its

00:03:53.979 --> 00:03:55.919
capacity to do harm.

00:03:55.919 --> 00:04:00.209
Of course, the most delicate part of this
proposed solution was securing the compliance

00:04:00.209 --> 00:04:02.209
of Rick Sanchez in the first place.

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:07.609
While many researchers would rather deal with
SCP-682 in its current state, rather than

00:04:07.609 --> 00:04:12.829
risk the involvement of such an unstable individual,
Bright was surprisingly optimistic about his

00:04:12.829 --> 00:04:15.420
chances to obtain Rick’s help.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:18.620
Maybe it was the fact that Dr. Bright had
always thought of himself as something of

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.900
a loose cannon by the Foundation’s standards,
but he wasn’t intimidated by Sanchez’s

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.730
brand of chaotic shenanigans.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:30.870
Also, because SCP-682 was one of the anomalies
that Dr. Bright was not permitted to make

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:36.560
contact with after the last incident, he felt
a sense of duty to contribute to the effort

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.800
of neutralizing it.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:42.750
If he could help solve one of the Foundation’s
biggest problems to date - even in an indirect

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:48.210
way - Bright would be able to enjoy an immense
sense of accomplishment and purpose in his

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:49.700
eternal life.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:54.770
Inspired by his own questionable genius, Dr.
Bright set about preparing for his confrontation

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.420
with Rick Sanchez.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:00.150
After all, Bright would be marching straight
into the mad scientist’s private fortress

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:05.120
- the Smith household - and if possible, he
would want to be at least twice as prepared

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.340
as Sanchez was.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.360
Dr. Bright’s first priority was selecting
an anomalous weapon that he could brandish

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.350
in case the diplomatic approach was a failure.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:18.980
After considering his vast array of options,
Bright eventually settled on SCP-3108 - also

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.730
known as The Nerfing Gun.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:25.430
While Sanchez was known to surprise both his
friends and foes by deploying never-before-seen

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:29.670
gizmos in the heat of the moment, Dr. Bright
could rest assured that with the Nerfing Gun

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:34.930
as his sidearm, any invention that Rick brought
to the table would instantly become less effective

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.870
after a few well-placed shots.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:41.270
Next, was the matter of keeping up with Rick
Sanchez in case the scientist decided to escape

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.640
from the conversation by opening a portal
to one of the other infinite realities he

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:46.870
had access to.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:51.150
While anomalies that could cross dimensions
were far from unheard of at the Foundation,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.840
Bright’s options for consistent and reliable
interdimensional transportation were severely

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:56.840
limited.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.211
Jack was starting to realize that there was
a reason why the formula for Rick’s portal

00:06:00.211 --> 00:06:04.150
fluid was so highly in-demand in the greater
multiverse.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:08.150
Whether or not he really was the smartest
being in the universe, it was clear that Rick

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:13.870
Sanchez had one advantage over ninety percent
of the anomalies on record: he had an unparalleled

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.720
knack for running away.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.680
Initially, Dr. Bright was planning to bluff
the scientist by arriving at his doorstep

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.440
with SCP-507 - the Reluctant Dimensional Traveler.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.650
The hapless and otherwise ordinary young man
did possess the potential to follow Rick into

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:31.980
any dimension that the portal gun could reach,
though because he had no control over when

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:36.920
or where his body would be transported, the
prospect of having him assist Dr. Bright in

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.820
chasing Rick was a massive gamble.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:44.710
SCP-507 also didn’t knowingly have the ability
to bring along other individuals in his unplanned

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:49.420
leaps through reality, and with the fact that
Dr. Bright had notoriously bad luck - the

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:54.240
chances of winding up in the blender dimension
would be much higher than usual even if a

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.389
shared dimension hop were possible.

00:06:56.389 --> 00:07:02.180
Dr. Bright thought to himself that maybe Sanchez
would know how to stabilize SCP-507’s relationship

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.700
with spacetime.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:06.560
Then he laughed to himself in quiet frustration.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:10.620
Was he already turning to Rick for the answers
to other anomalous problems when he hadn’t

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.000
even met with him yet.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:18.460
His concern was still with neutralizing SCP-682,
but somehow even that felt dimensions away

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.639
now.

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:24.290
Feeling a bit depressed, Dr. Bright was all
but ready to throw in the towel when an unexpected

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.370
volunteer expressed interest in Dr. Bright’s
plan.

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:32.190
It was none other than SCP-343 - God himself.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:36.380
God said to Dr. Bright that he had been aware
of Rick Sanchez prior to his confinement at

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:40.850
the Foundation, and knew the man to be lacking
in all forms of humility.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:45.700
He said that even when it came to the heavy
responsibilities of creation, Rick had a tendency

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:50.391
to view his own suffering in the same way
he viewed his supposed better qualities: as

00:07:50.391 --> 00:07:52.850
yet another competition he was winning.

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:58.320
To that end, SCP-343 believed that it was
important that he visit Sanchez alongside

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:02.490
Bright, in the hopes that a chance interaction
with the alleged creator of the universe might

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.980
humble the man if nothing else.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:09.900
More crucially, SCP-343 was able to do the
very thing that Dr. Bright required for this

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:14.919
plan to work: free and unrestricted interdimensional
travel.

00:08:14.919 --> 00:08:20.040
SCP-343 warned Dr. Bright that the use of
such powers may alarm his so-called next-door

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:24.840
neighbors in the other realities, but he also
assured the immortal researcher that the beings

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:29.480
that most closely resemble 343 himself tend
to be generally reasonable.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:34.270
Dr. Bright was a bit confused by that explanation,
but he was grateful to have such a powerful

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:39.000
and benevolent anomaly at his side if he was
to face Rick Sanchez.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:45.329
With SCP-3108 in his hand and SCP-343 ready
and willing to assist should the situation

00:08:45.329 --> 00:08:49.829
turn sour, Dr. Bright decided that his preparations
were complete.

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:54.259
He made his way to the Smith Household, where
Rick would be awaiting him.

00:08:54.259 --> 00:08:57.089
Fortunately, the man wasn’t that hard to
find.

00:08:57.089 --> 00:08:59.740
Probably because he wasn’t expecting company
that day.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:03.870
When Bright arrived at the house, the door
to the garage was already wide-open.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:08.160
Inside was Rick Sanchez tinkering with some
unknown piece of futuristic technology.

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:12.710
Dr. Bright knew better than to lead with any
questions about Rick’s new device, as the

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:15.360
response would probably be some kind of snarky
non-answer.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:21.579
Instead, he chose to approach casually with
SCP-3108 behind his back.

00:09:21.579 --> 00:09:27.980
At this time, SCP-343 had chosen to make himself
invisible, vowing to interfere only if Dr.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:31.029
Bright needed to pursue Sanchez through the
dimensions.

00:09:31.029 --> 00:09:35.050
Before Dr. Bright had even made it all the
way up the driveway, Sanchez indicated that

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.320
he was aware of the researcher’s presence.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:41.180
The rogue scientist didn’t even look up
from his work, and while Bright couldn’t

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:45.959
quite comprehend what had been said due to
an unexpected belch from Rick, he knew that

00:09:45.959 --> 00:09:48.470
he had been insulted somehow.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:52.920
Not one to be discouraged by mere words, Dr.
Bright introduced himself and explained that

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.810
he was from the SCP Foundation.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:59.930
He reminded Rick of his history with the Foundation,
and politely asked if Rick was interested

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.230
in doing some pro-bono work for them.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:03.630
To which, Rick snickered.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:08.740
It was clear that being vague wasn’t helping
his case, so Bright asked again, this time

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:13.660
laying out in more detail the task that the
research team wanted Rick to perform.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:18.579
Doing his best to avoid giving away any information
that might indirectly compromise the foundation,

00:10:18.579 --> 00:10:24.300
Dr. Bright explained SCP-682 and its capabilities
in the hopes that Rick might agree to see

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.920
the creature out of a sense of scientific
curiosity.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:32.430
Once again, Rick didn’t even look in Bright’s
direction before saying “It’s a big universe

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:35.640
and I’ve got better things to do than pick
a fight with some lizard.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:40.589
If you want my advice, toss that thing out
with the garbage somewhere and forget about

00:10:40.589 --> 00:10:41.589
it.

00:10:41.589 --> 00:10:44.220
That way, it’s not your problem, and it’s
definitely not mine.”

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.569
Dr. Bright wasn’t sure how to respond at
first.

00:10:46.569 --> 00:10:51.560
He had heard that Sanchez was unreasonable,
but he wasn’t expecting the man to suggest

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:55.009
that SCP-682 should be released from captivity.

00:10:55.009 --> 00:10:59.760
The recklessness of such a concept was shocking
for a seasoned Foundation researcher, but

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:05.730
there was something else: Rick Sanchez didn’t
seem at all phased by the existence of 682.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:09.629
The way that the man spoke made it sound like
even an indestructible monster was beneath

00:11:09.629 --> 00:11:10.629
him.

00:11:10.629 --> 00:11:14.180
Could it be possible that Sanchez had faced
far worse things before in his adventures

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:15.180
through the multiverse?

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:20.689
Or was he simply too apathetic to register
SCP-682 as a threat?

00:11:20.689 --> 00:11:22.279
He could also be a fool.

00:11:22.279 --> 00:11:25.839
Dr. Bright thought to himself, but he dismissed
that notion immediately.

00:11:25.839 --> 00:11:30.379
If there was one thing the Foundation knew
for sure about Rick Sanchez, it was that the

00:11:30.379 --> 00:11:34.459
man had to be some kind of genius - sane or
otherwise.

00:11:34.459 --> 00:11:39.990
Dr. Bright was intrigued, and at that moment,
that feeling got the better of him.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:44.949
He proceeded to explain the death toll that
SCP-682 was capable of: the inevitable loss

00:11:44.949 --> 00:11:48.769
of life which occurred every time the reptile
broke free of containment.

00:11:48.769 --> 00:11:54.200
Rick gave another dispassionate answer, “Again,
it sounds like your organization specializes

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:57.749
in taking things that would be better left
alone and making them into ‘you problems’.

00:11:57.749 --> 00:12:01.589
If that’s what lets you sleep at night,
I’m not going to stop you, but you can’t

00:12:01.589 --> 00:12:03.809
convince me that it’s a ‘me problem.’”

00:12:03.809 --> 00:12:05.510
Dr. Bright was at a loss.

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:11.089
Surely, Rick Sanchez knew that the sacrifices
made to keep SCP-682 from escaping the foundation

00:12:11.089 --> 00:12:14.890
were necessary to prevent innocent lives from
being stolen.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:19.490
The entire point of keeping anomalies secured
and contained was to protect humanity from

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:21.110
beings like 682.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:25.680
If there were a better way, especially regarding
one of the most deadly and malicious creatures

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:30.629
that the Foundation had ever come across,
naturally, any researcher would want to take

00:12:30.629 --> 00:12:31.629
it.

00:12:31.629 --> 00:12:35.759
And yet, here was Rick Sanchez, mocking everything
the foundation stood for.

00:12:35.759 --> 00:12:40.129
Dr. Bright had to laugh because he finally
understood who and what the man he was dealing

00:12:40.129 --> 00:12:42.290
with now really was.

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:46.959
As a former human turned immortal consciousness,
Dr. Bright had to reckon every day with the

00:12:46.959 --> 00:12:49.540
question of how to spend the rest of his endless
existence.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:55.769
There had been times since his mind was copied
into SCP-963 that Bright had been so consumed

00:12:55.769 --> 00:13:00.290
with boredom, he questioned whether it was
meaningful to do anything at all with his

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:01.290
days.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:05.059
After all, there would come a point in the
distant future where everything and everyone

00:13:05.059 --> 00:13:07.670
he ever knew would be completely gone.

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:11.879
The entire world and most of the people and
anomalies within it wouldn’t last forever,

00:13:11.879 --> 00:13:16.559
and he’d probably still be here long after
most everything else was gone.

00:13:16.559 --> 00:13:20.939
Until the necklace his mind was bound to was
somehow destroyed, Dr. Bright would live on

00:13:20.939 --> 00:13:25.339
indefinitely until everything in existence
turned to dust.

00:13:25.339 --> 00:13:29.119
Because of this heightened awareness of eternity,
Dr. Bright had forgotten what it was like

00:13:29.119 --> 00:13:33.749
to be on the other side of the nihilism he
felt daily: He had forgotten that everyone

00:13:33.749 --> 00:13:37.130
else in the universe was afraid of meeting
their end.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:38.930
Including Rick Sanchez.

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:42.570
That was why he couldn’t but laugh out loud
in front of that man.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:47.089
He was laughing because, for all of Sanchez’s
intelligence, the man was powerless against

00:13:47.089 --> 00:13:52.370
his own nihilistic apathy and the powerful
sense of worthlessness that came with it.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:56.811
Sanchez reacted swiftly to Bright’s laughter,
craning his neck towards the SCP researcher

00:13:56.811 --> 00:13:58.290
and asking “What was so funny?”

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:00.560
in a seemingly offended tone.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:05.839
Dr. Bright simply responded, “Oh, nothing”
and added that coming here was a mistake.

00:14:05.839 --> 00:14:09.940
It’s not as if Rick Sanchez was actually
capable of helping the Foundation deal with

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:10.940
SCP-682.

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:15.839
Dr. Bright made that remark with as much sarcasm
as he could muster, directly to Rick’s face.

00:14:15.839 --> 00:14:19.800
Rick was quick to snap back at Bright with
the assertion that he could totally deal with

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:23.360
their lizard problem: he just didn’t feel
motivated to.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.870
Just then, Rick’s grandson Morty Smith came
into the garage.

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:30.910
He was about to ask his grandfather for help
with him and his sister Summer’s homework

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:33.470
when he noticed Dr. Bright standing by.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.910
Morty took one look at the medallion around
Dr. Bright’s neck and immediately became

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:38.730
excited from sudden recognition.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:42.819
“Aww, geez, Rick, that’s Dr. Bright from
the SCP Foundation!”

00:14:42.819 --> 00:14:43.819
Morty said, excitedly.

00:14:43.819 --> 00:14:44.819
“Forget my homework!

00:14:44.819 --> 00:14:47.070
Are we doing an SCP adventure today?”

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.070
Rick groaned in disbelief.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:50.660
“No, we are not doing an SCP adventure.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.610
Because I don’t respect them or their weird
obsession with imprisoning stuff, and neither

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:54.610
should you.”

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:58.529
He belched loudly and turned back to his work
desk, but Morty’s expression turned angry,

00:14:58.529 --> 00:15:00.970
and it was clear that he wasn’t about to
leave.

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:01.970
“Typical, Rick.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:05.639
There’s finally an adventure I want to do,
and you’re acting like it’s lame!

00:15:05.639 --> 00:15:08.809
You know, a lot of people really enjoy SCPs!

00:15:08.809 --> 00:15:12.950
There’s even this Youtube channel called
SCP Explained that makes these really good

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:17.110
videos that explain the lore and tell some
awesome stories,” Morty said, directly into

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:18.720
the camera.

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:20.120
“Woof.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:22.240
Are you doing an ad for them right now, Morty?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.089
That’s pretty shameless,” Rick replied.

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:28.040
Dr. Bright got the feeling that these two
could go on for a while, and he also started

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.899
to get the impression that he was being ignored.

00:15:30.899 --> 00:15:35.439
He waited patiently for a lull in the banter,
but it didn’t seem to be happening anytime

00:15:35.439 --> 00:15:36.439
soon.

00:15:36.439 --> 00:15:38.939
Perhaps Dr. Bright could use this to his advantage.

00:15:38.939 --> 00:15:42.980
Rick Sanchez’ portal gun was lying on the
garage’s workbench not too far away from

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:44.949
where Dr. Bright was standing.

00:15:44.949 --> 00:15:50.569
One well-placed shot from SCP-3108 could be
sufficient to cut off Sanchez’ means of

00:15:50.569 --> 00:15:51.569
escape.

00:15:51.569 --> 00:15:56.179
All Dr. Bright had to do was line up the shot
and fire while Sanchez was distracted.

00:15:56.179 --> 00:16:00.490
Seeing just such an opportunity, Dr. Bright
moved the nerfing gun into position, but unfortunately

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:05.540
for him, Morty - the resident SCP expert of
the Smith family, as he was an avid subscriber

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:10.489
and watcher of SCP Explained - noticed what
he was holding and identified it immediately.

00:16:10.489 --> 00:16:11.730
“Careful, Rick!

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:14.560
Dr. Bright brought SCP-3108 with him!”

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:15.560
Morty shouted.

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:17.699
Rick responded, “Which one is that again?

00:16:17.699 --> 00:16:19.980
Is that the bird that causes separation anxiety?”

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:21.879
“No, that’s 3103!

00:16:21.879 --> 00:16:23.139
3108 is–”

00:16:23.139 --> 00:16:28.230
Dr. Bright fired SCP-3108 before Morty could
finish his sentence, but the boy was more

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:30.679
capable than Bright could have anticipated.

00:16:30.679 --> 00:16:34.709
Sanchez’s grandson dove recklessly into
the path of the projectile, shielding the

00:16:34.709 --> 00:16:39.179
portal gun with his body and immediately suffering
the anomalous effects of the nerfing gun:

00:16:39.179 --> 00:16:41.569
devolving into a neanderthal.

00:16:41.569 --> 00:16:45.529
Rick looked at Morty, who was now a caveman,
and became immediately enraged.

00:16:45.529 --> 00:16:50.889
And it was easy to understand why: nobody
uses Rick Sanchez’ grandson to test strange

00:16:50.889 --> 00:16:54.949
new inventions except for Rick Sanchez himself.

00:16:54.949 --> 00:16:58.889
Rick grabbed his portal gun from the workbench
and returned fire on Dr. Bright, creating

00:16:58.889 --> 00:17:03.589
two portals on the fly – one behind Dr.
Bright and the other in the path of the researcher’s

00:17:03.589 --> 00:17:04.839
second nerf round.

00:17:04.839 --> 00:17:08.360
The projectile zoomed through one portal and
out the other to collide with the back of

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:09.820
Dr. Bright’s head.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:13.640
Since his consciousness was contained inside
the medallion, Dr. Bright didn’t suffer

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:18.490
any mental changes as a result of being regressed
to a neanderthal, but the transformation did

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:23.820
grant him a newfound muscle mass and strength
only known to his primitive ancestors.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:25.270
And he was about to need it.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:29.390
Rick slammed a large cube onto the counter
that had a single large blue button on the

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:32.260
top, and as one must expect, pressed the button.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:36.440
Dr. Bright had never seen this before, but
this was one of Rick Sanchez’s other most

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:39.450
prized inventions: the Meeseeks box.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:43.850
The instant Sanchez pressed that button, an
unusual blue humanoid materialized into reality

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:45.830
from thin air.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.240
“I’m Mr. Meeseeks!

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:50.670
Look at me!” said the humanoid, apparently
known as Mr. Meeseeks.

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:52.860
“Get rid of that guy!”

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:57.020
Rick ordered, and immediately Mr. Meeseeks
began sprinting towards the researcher with

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:59.360
single-minded determination.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:05.950
Dr. Bright only had time to fire a single
shot from SCP-3108 before Mr. Meeseeks grabbed

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:09.140
him by the wrists and tried to wrestle the
nerfing pistol away.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:13.820
It was a smart move on Bright’s part, because
the nerf round struck the Meeseeks box directly

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:18.790
- rendering it near useless as the exterior
turned red and the word “Kirkland” appeared

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:20.270
on the box’s side.

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:23.250
Annoyed, Rick pushed the Meeseeks box into
the trash.

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:26.580
While he could rest assured that he wouldn’t
have to contend with another Mr. Meeseeks,

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.980
it was taking all of Dr. Bright’s current
caveman strength to prevent the blue humanoid

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.360
from disarming him.

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:36.420
Desperate to gain some advantage over Sanchez
and his inventions, Dr. Bright called for

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:41.670
help from SCP-343, which Rick misinterpreted
as the researcher praying to be spared from

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:43.490
the mad genius’ wrath.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:48.900
Sanchez was shocked when 343 became visible
and immediately appeared before Mr. Meeseeks.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:54.800
“I release you from your quest for purpose,”
God said to Mr. Meeseeks, and a grin spread

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.220
over the humanoid’s face.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:19:01.200
In the next moment, Mr. Meeseeks was gone,
returned to the void of nonexistence.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.590
God then turned to Rick Sanchez with a stern
but fatherly look.

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:05.670
Rick was unamused.

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:07.270
“Oh, would you look at that?

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:10.660
Dr. Bright has a literal God on his side,”
Rick quipped sarcastically.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:14.990
“What’s next, are you going to use the
power of anime on me?”

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:19.180
God wiggled his fingers and in a flash of
light… both Morty and Dr. Bright were restored

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:23.350
to their original human selves, or in Bright’s
case: human in appearance.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.040
Morty sputtered, “Ahh, Rick, I’m freaking
out!

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:29.880
I just went through thousands of years of
human evolution.

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:30.922
I need to lie down.”

00:19:30.922 --> 00:19:34.210
While Dr. Bright was grateful that his current
body felt more like himself again, he had

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:38.120
been counting on God to help him defeat Rick
Sanchez if things had gone bad.

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:41.780
And from the looks of it, the situation was
still pretty untenable.

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:45.580
That’s when Dr. Bright noticed that Rick
was no longer trying to fight back.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:49.300
Instead, the rogue scientist was comforting
his grandson after the painful process of

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:50.680
two-way evolution.

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:55.900
Perhaps there was more to this man than his
devil-may-care antics and pessimistic outlook?

00:19:55.900 --> 00:20:00.130
After giving Morty’s physical and mental
state the bare minimum level of consideration,

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.080
Rick turned to Dr. Bright and said:

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:06.620
“Hey, so, SCP guys, we’re going have to
do a rain check on this whole shebang until

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:07.690
Morty is feeling better.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:13.040
I guess he really wanted to do an SCP adventure,
so I guess we’ll pencil you into our busy

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:14.580
Rick and Morty adventure schedule.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:18.250
Just don’t bug us about it or make it a
big deal and we won’t either.”

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:19.820
Dr. Bright couldn’t help but smile.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:24.980
He may not have gotten Rick to neutralize
SCP-382, but he just might have secured a

00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:28.760
valuable asset for the foundation to call
upon in the future.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:31.890
And that’s at least like half a win, right?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:36.190
Now go check out “HILARIOUS List of Things
Dr. Bright is Not Allowed to Do!” and “SCP

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:39.510
Edition - Weirdest Things on Amazon - Dr Bright's
Great Idea!”

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:41.270
for more Dr. Bright adventures!

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:42.850
Wubba lubba dub dub!

